nse_decision:{mode,reason,evidence_event_ids:[]}. All summaries/reasons/next_action must be nonempty plain text. stage is undetermined/investigation/awaiting_customer/awaiting_internal/options_offered/awaiting_acceptance/awaiting_return/awaiting_document_review/refund_ready/refund_submitted/resolved. waiting_for is none/customer/internal. Cite actual integer event IDs available in ticket messages/related_messages; decision MUST include trigger_event_id. mode is reply (substantive), acknowledge (brief useful confirmation), or no_reply (waiting/resolved with no helpful outgoing content). Default to reply when uncertain. acknowledge/no_reply allowed only when ALL planned intents are conversation_update and ALL action_stage values are information. Never suppress a new question, objection, acceptance requiring action or material evidence review. no_reply MUST also cite prior agent context and be justified with a concrete internal next_action; use no_reply only with complete history. For 11104-like damaged-parcel video promise, prefer acknowledge to clarify the video scope and accept Saturday; do not treat a future video as received. For thanks after a complete resolution with no remaining question, no_reply may be appropriate. points may cite event:<integer ID> as communication evidence; these refs do not prove operational actions. follow_up_note is a human follow-up suggestion or quoted commitment, not a scheduled task. This is an evidence-backed assessment, not an authoritative persisted order/refund state.",user_prompt:JSON.stringify({ticket:context.ticket,operator_guidance:context.operator_guidance,plan:resolved.plan,facts:resolved.facts,missing_facts:resolved.missing_facts,policies})}}];

